WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.920
It’s been a busy first week since Elon Musk
took control of Twitter on October 27th.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.130
He appointed himself CEO.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.880
Make that “Chief Twit”

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.210
Or Twitter complaint hotline operator.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.720
There were plenty of complaints when Musk
said people would have to start paying $8

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.960
a month to keep their blue check mark or to
get one.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.980
AOC wasn’t too happy.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.410
Musk’s response to the Congresswoman?

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.750
Pay up.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.900
The SpaceX and Tesla CEO didn’t waste any
time getting down to business.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.760
He ousted Twitter’s nine board of directors
to become the sole director, though he says

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.530
being sole director is temporary.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:44.480
He also started to trim the fat and is reportedly
planning on eliminating nearly half of Twitter’s

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.990
workforce, or 3,700 jobs, according to Bloomberg.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:55.340
These two guys pretended to be laid-off employees…and
gave their names as Rahul Ligma and Daniel

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.250
Johnson to reporters who fell for their prank.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:04.280
But Musk did really start day one as chief
of Twitter by firing top Twitter executives.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:09.220
CEO Parag Agrawal got the boot
So did Chief Financial Officer Ned Segal

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.750
And…legal affairs and policy executive Vijaya
Gadde.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:19.220
Gadde was reportedly instrumental in permanently
banning Donald Trump from the platform for

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.320
controversial tweets related to the Capitol
Hill riot in January 2021.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.920
Musk said banning the former U.S. president
was “a morally bad decision”.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.720
Everyone is wondering whether the former President
will be back on Twitter.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.880
Musk mused that if he “had a dollar for
every time someone asked (him) if Trump is

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.240
coming back on this platform, Twitter would
be minting money!”

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.759
Before any big changes, he says “Twitter
will be forming a content moderation council

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:48.330
with widely diverse viewpoints.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:54.100
No major content decisions or account reinstatements
will happen before that council convenes.”

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.799
He said the process would take “at least
a few more weeks”.

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:02.510
Musk did buy the platform because he’s a
self-described “free speech absolutist”

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:07.189
Who believes Twitter should be “the digital
town square” but thinks it has gone “too

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:09.899
far in squashing dissenting opinions.”

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:14.600
The final straw appears to have been when
Twitter suspended the Babylon Bee, a Christian

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:20.769
satire account that named U.S. Assistant Secretary
for Health Dr. Rachel Levine its “Man of

00:02:20.769 --> 00:02:21.830
the Year”.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.920
Many who are viewed as conservative feel they’ve
been unfairly targeted by Twitter.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.440
Clinical psychologist Jordan Peterson had
his account suspended over his post about

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.400
transgender actor Elliot Page, formerly Ellen
Page.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.819
But the suspension will not be lifted unless
I delete the “hateful” tweet in question,

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:43.019
and I would rather die than do that.

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:47.730
Musk replied to Peterson’s daughter that
“Anyone suspended for minor &amp; dubious reasons

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.269
will be freed from Twitter jail”.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:53.610
Now that he’s in charge, Elon Musk won’t
only be freeing people from Twitter jail.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:58.060
Just like his ambitions for his other companies,
SpaceX and Tesla, he has far bigger plans

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.120
for the platform.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.760
In his view, Twitter is “an accelerant to
creating X, the everything app.”

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.750
There’s speculation that he wants to replicate
the success of WeChat, which has basically

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.090
become the everything app in China.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:16.040
When YouTuber Steven Mark Ryan of Solving
the Money Problem pointed out it’s “INSANE

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.040
that Twitter has not currently implemented
a YouTube clone” - Musk responded with a

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.040
wink.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.150
Could we see creators monetizing videos on
Twitter?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:29.720
Musk polled people to ask if they wanted to
bring back Vine, the short video-sharing app

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.490
that Twitter shut down in 2016.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:36.129
He talked about it being a possible competitor
for TikTok.

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:39.360
All these plans rely on good engineering.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.560
Musk reportedly sent in his trusted Tesla
engineers to inspect Twitter’s code to assess

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.930
the company's needs.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:49.790
They’ll have to tackle the problem of fake
and spam accounts.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:55.000
In fact, Musk tried to get out of buying Twitter,
believing it wasn’t worth the $44 billion

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.030
he offered to take it private…due to the
number of spam bots.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:04.550
Musk believes the way to defeat the bots while
also making money for Twitter is by charging

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.040
you if you want this blue check mark.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.349
This is arguably his most controversial move
during week one.

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:17.000
The blue verification badge has become a status
symbol granted to journalists, celebrities,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.500
politicians, some of whom were furious when
they heard they’d have to pay $19.99 a month

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.800
to keep their blue tick as reported by The
Verge.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.990
Musk replied to an unhappy Stephen King that
Twitter needs to pay the bills somehow.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.830
And wondered if the horror author might be
willing to dish out $8 instead.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:40.470
He called the current system for who has and
doesn’t have the blue tick is “BS” and

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.630
that charging $8 a month for anyone who wants
it would mean more “power to the people”.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:50.650
This would be part of the Twitter Blue subscription
service which comes with other benefits.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.350
Although Musk has long boasted that Tesla
does not pay for advertising, advertising

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.280
has been crucial to Twitter’s survival.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.880
General Motors temporarily pulled ads from
Twitter following the takeover.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:08.030
Musk tried to reassure advertisers that Twitter
would be a respected advertising platform.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:13.380
In an open letter, he stressed that he doesn’t
want Twitter to “become a free-for-all hellscape,

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.830
where anything can be said with no consequences!”

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:20.500
He also said he bought Twitter “to help
humanity, whom I love.”

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.440
Will people love the new Twitter?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.970
Users have begun to notice some changes.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.310
When the White House boasted seniors are getting
the biggest social security increase in a

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:35.910
decade thanks to President Biden, context
checkers pointed out it’s because inflation

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.789
has been the highest in decades.

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:41.020
The White House then deleted the tweet.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.229
Musk can only hope that Twitter soars to new
heights, like his rocket company SpaceX.

00:05:46.229 --> 00:05:49.350
Though some have vowed to leave.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:54.320
However you feel, let that sink in, that a
new boss is in town.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.740
Can’t help it, let that sink in.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:01.810
Twitter is now a private company and will
no longer be listed on the New York stock

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:02.810
exchange.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:07.090
However, millions of investors have already
dropped their shares in the last few months,

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.430
as it got too volatile.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.990
And their caution is well-founded;

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:14.480
The classic 60/40 portfolio of stocks and
bonds,

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.940
The go-to investing method for decades,

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.090
has lost around 34% this year.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:26.190
As a result, Goldman Sachs says portfolios
need to be rebalanced, to avoid further losses.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:31.580
They highlight the importance of investing
in real assets that have historically outperformed

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.000
in volatile conditions.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.580
Assets like fine art.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.370
And it’s why Masterworks is seeing increased
demand this year.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.400
Masterworks lets you invest in multimillion-dollar
paintings, from legends like Picasso.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.160
You can buy shares in these paintings without
owning millions yourself.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.300
These are not NFTs.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:56.030
Contemporary art has outpaced the S&amp;P 500
by 131%, for the last 26 years.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.060
Even during the bull market of the last decade.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:06.300
In October, Masterworks sold this painting
by George Condo for a 21.5% net return.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:12.660
In fact, six of Masterworks’ seven sales
have brought in over 20% net returns.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.570
Masterworks has a waitlist to join their 550,000-plus
members.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:22.050
But you can skip the waitlist by clicking
the custom link in the description.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:30.100
That’s masterworks.art/newsthink, masterworks.art/newsthink
to get started investing in fine art.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.160
Thanks for watching.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.090
For Newsthink, I’m Cindy Pom.

